IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `nz-interpretation-time`

-- Legislation Act 2019 (New Zealand) -- LAYER 1: PART 2, PURPOSES, APPLICATION AND GENERAL PRINCIPLES (ss 8 to 12).
-- s 8 (the purposes of Part 2) is not operative and carries no rule: see the coverage table in NOTES.md.

§ `Section 9 -- Application of this Part`

-- src:93 | 9 Application of this Part
-- src:94 | A provision of this Part applies to legislation that is part of the laws of New Zealand unless—
-- src:95 | the legislation provides otherwise; or
-- src:96 | the context of the legislation requires a different interpretation.
-- (1) A provision of this Part applies to legislation that is part of the laws of New Zealand unless the legislation provides
-- otherwise or its context requires a different interpretation. (2) The provisions of this Part also apply to the interpretation of this Act.
-- "the context ... requires a different interpretation" is a judgment the text leaves to the reader: it is taken as an input.
@ref Legislation Act 2019 s 9(1) (src:93-96)
GIVEN `the legislation is part of the laws of New Zealand` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the legislation provides otherwise` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the context of the legislation requires a different interpretation` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`a provision of Part 2 applies to the legislation` `the legislation is part of the laws of New Zealand` `the legislation provides otherwise` `the context of the legislation requires a different interpretation` MEANS
        `the legislation is part of the laws of New Zealand`
    AND (NOT `the legislation provides otherwise`)
    AND (NOT `the context of the legislation requires a different interpretation`)

-- (2) This Act is itself legislation to which Part 2 is applied; subsection (1) still decides whether a given provision applies to it.
-- src:97 | The provisions of this Part also apply to the interpretation of this Act.
@ref Legislation Act 2019 s 9(2) (src:97)
GIVEN `the legislation is this Act` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`Part 2 is applied to the interpretation of` `the legislation is this Act` MEANS `the legislation is this Act`

§ `Section 10 -- How to ascertain meaning of legislation`

DECLARE `What meaning is ascertained from` IS ONE OF
    `the text of the legislation`
    `the purpose of the legislation`
    `the context of the legislation`

DECLARE `Kind of indication` IS ONE OF
    `a preamble`
    `a table of contents`
    `a heading`
    `a diagram`
    `a graphic`
    `an example`
    `explanatory material`
    `the organisation and format of the legislation`
    `the organisation of the legislation`
    `the format of the legislation`
    `another indication`

-- src:99 | 10 How to ascertain meaning of legislation
-- src:100 | The meaning of legislation must be ascertained from its text and in the light of its purpose and its context.
-- (1) The meaning of legislation must be ascertained from its text and in the light of its purpose and its context.
@ref Legislation Act 2019 s 10(1) (src:99-100)
GIVEN source IS A `What meaning is ascertained from`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`the meaning of legislation must be ascertained from` source MEANS
    CONSIDER source
    WHEN `the text of the legislation` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `the purpose of the legislation` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `the context of the legislation` THEN TRUE

-- (2) Subsection (1) applies whether or not the legislation's purpose is stated in the legislation.
-- src:101 | Subsection (1) applies whether or not the legislation’s purpose is stated in the legislation.
@ref Legislation Act 2019 s 10(2) (src:101)
GIVEN `the purpose is stated in the legislation` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`the purpose is used to ascertain the meaning` `the purpose is stated in the legislation` MEANS TRUE

-- (3) The text of legislation includes the indications provided in the legislation. (4) Examples of those indications are
-- preambles, a table of contents, headings, diagrams, graphics, examples and explanatory material, and the organisation and format.
-- "Examples of" is not a closed list: any other indication provided in the legislation is text too.
-- src:102 | The text of legislation includes the indications provided in the legislation.
-- src:103 | Examples of those indications are preambles, a table of contents, headings, diagrams, graphics, examples and explanatory material, and the organisation and format of the legislation.
@ref Legislation Act 2019 s 10(3) and (4) (src:102-103)
GIVEN indication IS A `Kind of indication`
      `it is provided in the legislation` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`an indication is part of the text of the legislation` indication `it is provided in the legislation` MEANS
    `it is provided in the legislation`

§ `Section 11 -- Legislation applies to circumstances as they arise`

-- src:104 | 11 Legislation applies to circumstances as they arise
-- src:105 | Legislation applies to circumstances as they arise.
-- Legislation applies to a circumstance on the day the circumstance arises if the legislation is in force that day: from the day it
-- comes into force and, if it is repealed on a particular day, up to the day before (s 39). A day is the unit; the moment of day is s 27.
@ref Legislation Act 2019 s 11 (src:104-105)
GIVEN `the day the circumstance arises` IS A DATE
      `the day the legislation comes into force` IS A DATE
      `the day it is repealed` IS A MAYBE DATE
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`legislation applies to a circumstance as it arises` `the day the circumstance arises` `the day the legislation comes into force` `the day it is repealed` MEANS
        `the day the circumstance arises` AT LEAST `the day the legislation comes into force`
    AND CONSIDER `the day it is repealed`
        WHEN NOTHING THEN TRUE
        WHEN JUST repealDay THEN `legislation expressed to be repealed on` repealDay `is still in force on` `the day the circumstance arises`

§ `Section 12 -- Legislation does not have retrospective effect`

DECLARE `Application to a past circumstance` IS ONE OF
    `The legislation applies`
    `The legislation does not apply: no retrospective effect`

-- src:106 | 12 Legislation does not have retrospective effect
-- src:107 | Legislation does not have retrospective effect.
-- s 12 is a provision of Part 2, so s 9(1)(a) lets legislation provide otherwise (fork F7).
@ref Legislation Act 2019 s 12 (src:106-107)
GIVEN `the day the circumstance arose` IS A DATE
      `the day the legislation came into force` IS A DATE
      `the legislation provides otherwise` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A `Application to a past circumstance`
`whether the legislation applies to a circumstance that arose on` `the day the circumstance arose` `when it came into force on` `the day the legislation came into force` `and it provides otherwise` `the legislation provides otherwise` MEANS
    IF     (`the day the circumstance arose` LESS THAN `the day the legislation came into force`)
       AND (NOT `the legislation provides otherwise`)
    THEN `The legislation does not apply: no retrospective effect`
    ELSE `The legislation applies`
